      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Doctors Without Borders USA excels in financial management and transparency. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"3\">over $767 million in revenue</cite> while keeping fundraising costs low at <cite id=\"1\">$0.15 per $1 raised</cite>. Their governance is supported by an <cite id=\"1\">independent board of 13 members</cite>, with <cite id=\"1\">91% independence</cite> reported. This oversight ensures that resources are directed toward their core mission of <cite id=\"1\">alleviating suffering and protecting life</cite> in the world's most dangerous regions."
      ],
      "summary": "Doctors Without Borders USA (MSF) provides rapid medical relief for people facing war, disease, and natural disasters. As a major international humanitarian institution, the organization reported <cite id=\"3\">$767,362,916 in total revenue</cite> in FY2024. This funding supports a wide array of services, including <cite id=\"1\">emergency medical response, infectious disease control, and nutritional support</cite>. The charity is highly regarded for its operational excellence, maintaining a <cite id=\"1\">97/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>. This rating reflects a strong commitment to both financial health and accountability. MSF focuses on direct service delivery, often operating in regions where local health systems have collapsed. For example, the organization has demonstrated its capacity by performing <cite id=\"4\">4,000 surgeries</cite> and distributing <cite id=\"4\">14,000 tents</cite> during major crisis responses. While the charity is a mainstream global health leader, it maintains <cite id=\"2\">high alignment with Muslim donor priorities</cite> by serving vulnerable populations in many Muslim-majority regions. However, donors should note that this organization is <cite id=\"2\">Sadaqah-eligible only</cite>. Financially, the organization is efficient, spending <cite id=\"1\">$0.15 to raise every $1</cite>, which is well within industry standards for large-scale relief operations.",
